### Description

The agno framework does not seem to use the right tool_choice when using pydantic model to get structured output:

it should use the provided pydantic model as tool_choice as described here.

* Claude models: https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/agents-and-tools/tool-use/implement-tool-use#forcing-tool-use
* Nova models: https://docs.aws.amazon.com/nova/latest/userguide/tool-choice.html

### Steps to Reproduce

* Run structured output with pydantic model and agno
* Observe the llm request, which looks like this
```
     "toolConfig": {
                "tools": [
                    {
                        "toolSpec": {
                            "name": "MyOutputModel",
                            "description": "my great tool schema",
                            "inputSchema": {
                                "json": {
                                    "type": "object",
                                    "title": "MyOutputModel",
                                    ...
                            }
                        }
                    }
                ],
                "toolChoice": {
                    "auto": {}
                }
            }
```

it should look like this though
```
tool_config = {
    "toolChoice": {
        "tool": { "name" : "MyOutputModel"}
    },
    "tools": [
        {...
```

### Agent Configuration (if applicable)

_No response_

### Expected Behavior

```
tool_config = {
    "toolChoice": {
        "tool": { "name" : "MyOutputModel"}
    },
    "tools": [
        {...
```

### Actual Behavior

```
      "toolChoice": {
                    "auto": {}
                }
```

### Screenshots or Logs (if applicable)

no logs required

### Environment

```markdown
independent of environment
```

### Possible Solutions (optional)

_No response_

### Additional Context

_No response_

### Description

In Agno v2.x, when media (e.g., images or videos) is generated via tools like create_image, the internal method `_handle_function_call_media`  will append a user message containing image to the conversation messages.

Source code:
https://github.com/agno-agi/agno/blob/795d4137cf46a86da0ec514d496f5d0521ad93e8/libs/agno/agno/models/base.py#L1718-L1726

If the underlying model is non-multimodal, it cannot process image objects in the message payload — resulting in an inference error during subsequent turns.

### Steps to Reproduce

1. Create an Agent configured with a media-generating tool (e.g., DalleTools or create_image).
2. Connect to AgentOS
3. Input Draw me a dog. → Tool generates image, `_handle_function_call_media` append image into context.
4. Model throws inference error.

### Agent Configuration (if applicable)

```python
from agno.agent import Agent
from agno.tools.dalle import DalleTools

agent = Agent(
    model=OpenAILike(id="my_non_multimodal_model"),
    tools=[DalleTools()],
    name="DALL-E Image Generator",
    add_history_to_context=True,
)

agent.print_response(
    "Draw me a dog", markdown=True,
)

agent.print_response(
    "Hello", markdown=True
)
```

### Expected Behavior

Perhaps we can use a flag like Agent's `send_media_to_model=True` for non-multimodal models?

I’m also curious — why does `_handle_function_call_media` add a follow-up "user" message instead of a "tool"? 

### Actual Behavior

The input message payload:
```
{
    "messages": [
        {
            "content": "<additional_information>\n- Use markdown to format your answers.\n</additional_information>",
            "role": "system"
        },
        {
            "content": "Draw me a dog",
            "role": "user"
        },
        {
            "content": "",
            "role": "assistant",
            "tool_calls": [
                {
                    "id": "chatcmpl-tool-61ff370479bf4751b423e043a29fe679",
                    "type": "function",
                    "function": {
                        "name": "create_image",
                        "arguments": "{\"prompt\": \"a cute dog\"}"
                    }
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "content": "Image has been generated at the URL https://machinelearningknowledge.ai/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/image2.jpg \n",
            "role": "tool",
            "tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-61ff370479bf4751b423e043a29fe679"
        },
        {
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Take note of the following content"
                },
                {
                    "type": "image_url",
                    "image_url": {
                        "url": "https://machinelearningknowledge.ai/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/image2.jpg "
                    }
                }
            ],
            "role": "user"
        }
    ]
}
```

