Body:
### Description

During AGUI calls, the agent starts looping when trying to generate the followup message after the frontend tool rendered its component.

### Steps to Reproduce

1. Setup a frontend with CopilotKit
2. Run a tool that requires both frontend or MCP/backend tool execution

### Agent Configuration (if applicable)

tool for the frontend action
```python
from typing import List, Optional

from agno.tools import tool
from pydantic import BaseModel, Field


class DataPoint(BaseModel):
    """A single data point used to generate the chart."""

    ts: str = Field(
        ...,
        description="The x axis value representing the timestamp of the data point.",
    )
    v1: float = Field(..., alias="1", description="The y value of the data point.")
    v2: Optional[float] = Field(
        None,
        alias="2",
        description="The secondary y value of the data point. (OPTIONAL)",
    )
    v3: Optional[float] = Field(
        None,
        alias="3",
        description="The tertiary y value of the data point. (OPTIONAL)",
    )
    v4: Optional[float] = Field(
        None,
        alias="4",
        description="The quaternary y value of the data point. (OPTIONAL)",
    )
    v5: Optional[float] = Field(
        None, alias="5", description="The quinary y value of the data point. (OPTIONAL)"
    )
    v6: Optional[float] = Field(
        None, alias="6", description="The senary y value of the data point. (OPTIONAL)"
    )

    model_config = {
        "populate_by_name": True,
        "validate_by_name": True,
    }


class ChartData(BaseModel):
    """Chart configuration and data."""

    title: str = Field(..., description="The title of the chart.")
    labels: List[str] = Field(..., description="The labels for the chart data.")
    suffix: str = Field(..., description="The suffix appended to displayed values.")
    data: List[DataPoint] = Field(
        ..., description="The data points used to generate the chart."
    )


@tool(external_execution=True)
def generate_chart(
    title: str,  # pylint: disable=unused-argument
    labels: list[str],  # pylint: disable=unused-argument
    suffix: str,  # pylint: disable=unused-argument
    data: list[DataPoint],  # pylint: disable=unused-argument
) -> ChartData:  # pylint: disable=unused-argument
    """
    Generate charts or plots for the user by automatically retrieving raw data
      from available *_raw_data tools. This tool should:
        - Select the appropriate *_raw_data tool to fetch the underlying dataset.
        - Extract KPI data exclusively from properties in the response that are prefixed with "h_".
        - Use the extracted KPI data to generate the requested chart.
        - Explain it clearly if requested.
        - If no *_raw_data tool is suitable, return a helpful message.
        - Do not generate an image, the chart rendering is handled by the front end.
    ### Important Guidelines:
        - Always call the most relevant *_raw_data tool before generating the chart.
        - Only use properties starting with "h_" from the tool's response when preparing data for visualization.
        - Do not invent or simulate data; only use results from *_raw_data tools.
        - Use user's locale and timezone for date formatting and follow ups generation.
        - Label axes, labels, and titles appropriately based on the dataset context.
        - If data is missing, incomplete, or no "h_" properties are found, inform the user instead of making assumptions.
    """
```

frontend component
```react
const AgentChartTool = () => {
  const { t } = useTranslation();
  useCopilotAction({
    name: "generate_chart",
    parameters: [
      {
        description: "The title of the chart.",
        name: "title",
        type: "string",
      },
      {
        description: "The labels of the values being measured.",
        name: "labels",
        type: "string[]",
      },
      {
        description:
          "The suffix to append to the y axis values, e.g. kW, kWh, etc.",
        name: "suffix",
        type: "string",
      },
      {
        attributes: [
          {
            description:
              "The x axis value representing the timestamp of the data point.",
            name: "ts",
            type: "string",
          },
          {
            description: "The y value of the data point.",
            name: "1",
            type: "number",
          },
          {
            description: "The secondary y value of the data point. (OPTIONAL)",
            name: "2",
            type: "number",
          },
          {
            description: "The tertiary y value of the data point. (OPTIONAL)",
            name: "3",
            type: "number",
          },
          {
            description: "The quaternary y value of the data point. (OPTIONAL)",
            name: "4",
            type: "number",
          },
          {
            description: "The quinary y value of the data point. (OPTIONAL)",
            name: "5",
            type: "number",
          },
          {
            description: "The senary y value of the data point. (OPTIONAL)",
            name: "6",
            type: "number",
          },
        ],
        description: "An array of data points to generate the chart from.",
        name: "data",
        type: "object[]",
      },
    ],
    render: ({ args }) => {
      if (!args.data || args.data.length === 0) {
        return (
          <div className="flex items-center justify-center space-x-4 rounded-lg p-4">
            <div>No data available to generate chart.</div>
          </div>
        );
      }

      const numerOfValues = Object.keys(args.data[0] || {}).filter((k) =>
        ["1", "2", "3", "4", "5", "6"].includes(k)
      ).length;

      const startDate = DateTime.fromISO(args.data?.[0]?.ts || "").toJSDate();
      const endDate = DateTime.fromISO(args.data.at(-1)?.ts ?? "").toJSDate();

      return (
        <Card
          actions={[
            {
              icon: <Download />,
              label: "Download CSV",
              onClick: () => {
                exportToCSV(
                  [
                    "ts",
                    ...(args.labels ||
                      new Array(numerOfValues)
                        .fill(0)
                        .map((_, i) => (i + 1).toString())),
                  ],
                  args.data?.map((d) => [
                    d.ts,
                    ...new Array(numerOfValues)
                      .fill(0)
                      .map((_, i) => d[i + 1] || 0),
                  ]),
                  "chart-data"
                );
              },
            },
          ]}
          title={args.title || t("chart")}
        >
          <BarChart
            config={new Array(numerOfValues).fill(0).reduce(
              (acc, _, i) => ({
                // biome-ignore lint/performance/noAccumulatingSpread: .
                ...acc,
                [(i + 1).toString()]: {
                  label: args.labels?.[i] || `${"value"} ${i + 1}`,
                },
              }),
              {}
            )}
            data={
              args.data?.map((d) => ({
                ...new Array(numerOfValues).fill(0).reduce(
                  (acc, _, i) => ({
                    // biome-ignore lint/performance/noAccumulatingSpread: .
                    ...acc,
                    [(i + 1).toString()]: roundToDecimal(d[i + 1] || 0, 2),
                  }),
                  {}
                ),
                x: d.ts,
              })) || []
            }
            suffix={args.suffix || ""}
            tickFormatter={(value) =>
              DateTime.fromISO(value).toFormat(
                getDateGranularity(startDate, endDate || startDate)
              )
            }
          />
        </Card>
      );
    },
  });
  return null;
};
```

### Expected Behavior

It should run fine

### Actual Behavior

The agent enters in a loop.

