In the agent chat in the cloud ADE using Chrome, when a response is streaming in, I can't scroll up to read earlier messages. The chat immediately pulls me back to the bottom with every new token.

Pretty annoying when you want to check something from earlier in the conversation while waiting for a long response. It's a standard pattern in most chat apps is to pause auto-scroll when user scrolls up.

I ran some diagnostics in the console and the code is unconditionally setting `scrollTop = scrollHeight` on every DOM mutation during streaming. The `.agent-messenger-scroll` container gets forced to bottom regardless of where you've scrolled.

From the logs:
```
scrollTop SET to: 8781
// Coming from 9143-b57f7c6d4712908a.js
```

Happens on every chunk that comes in.

## Quick fix

Just need to track whether user is near the bottom before auto-scrolling:

```typescript
const distanceFromBottom = 
  container.scrollHeight - container.scrollTop - container.clientHeight;

// Only auto-scroll if already at bottom
if (distanceFromBottom < 100) {
  container.scrollTop = container.scrollHeight;
}
```

Tested a client-side version of this and it works fine - stays scrolled up when you scroll up, resumes auto-scroll when you go back to bottom.

Should be a straightforward fix - the logic is isolated to the scroll behavior.

